1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,440
<i>You said the Crow Club takes secret jobs</i>
<i>and can solve any problem.</i>

2
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,400
<i>Is that true or just an exaggeration?</i>

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,200
<i>Tomorrow, a client will come</i>
<i>to discuss a job with us.</i>

4
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,040
The client just wants you

5
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:18,240
<i>to negotiate with</i>
<i>the ghost that's following him.</i>

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,600
I'm forming a band to make our debut.

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,600
<i>I want to invite you to join the band.</i>

8
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,240
I've decided.

9
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:25,960
<i>I'll use him as the model</i>
<i>for the male lead in my novel.</i>

10
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:27,760
<i>He's my client?</i>

11
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,360
I won't take a client like him.

12
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,400
<i>But for this…</i>

13
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,280
<i>You're the only one who can help me.</i>

14
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,080
<i>It's time for me to let the clients know</i>

15
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,920
<i>whether you'll take the jobs.</i>

16
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:52,960
Why is it so tight?

17
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,400
You're really struggling, huh?

18
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,120
Hey!

19
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,560
EDITOR

20
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:31,120
If you don't want to do it,
why take the job?

21
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,280
Because I don't want to lose.

22
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:36,000
If I don't take this job,

23
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:38,000
Yoyeh will think that I…

24
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:40,440
still haven't moved on from him.

25
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:42,120
Well, have you really moved on?

26
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:49,640
Anyone could guess
in a situation like this.

27
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:53,840
He's willing to work
with the ex he hates again.

28
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:56,640
Dear Vann.

29
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:59,240
Just wait and see Tangmo.

30
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,560
Old flames are bound to reignite.

31
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,760
If you don't like it, just turn him down.

32
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,240
Why make it so complicated?

33
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,240
If I don't want to do it, I say no.

34
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,480
What's so hard about that?

35
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,760
You never care about anything.

36
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:21,200
Of course you'd say that.

37
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,560
True.

38
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,880
If Talay ever took a job,

39
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,080
the sun would rise in the west.

40
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,840
Vann, your job starts today.

41
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,560
Why haven't you left yet?

42
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,640
Come on.

43
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:36,960
You only kick me out
because I'm the youngest.

44
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:40,360
When the others are loud,
you never say anything to them.

45
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,120
I say it in my head, but no one hears it.

46
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:48,080
So, did you get a job, Phatee?

47
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:57,160
If we don't expect anything,
we won't be disappointed.

48
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,960
Whatever we ask him,

49
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:01,160
we never get an answer.

50
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:04,360
What about you?

51
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,760
Can you handle
a ghost-hunting job like this?

52
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,200
I took the job,

53
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,800
so I have to solve
the problem for my client.

54
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:12,680
I don't care what I have to do.

55
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:13,880
But one thing's for sure,

56
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,320
I'm going to finish the job.

57
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:19,760
That one million baht…

58
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:23,200
has to be mine.

59
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:35,080
Thank you for taking this job.

60
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:37,920
No problem.

61
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:40,040
I just feel sorry for you.

62
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,400
I can't stand seeing anyone in trouble.

63
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,560
And you said you'd pay me one million.

64
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,080
You really have the money
to pay me, right?

65
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,400
Wait a moment.

66
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,400
Shit.

67
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:06,640
Having eight figures in your account…

68
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,920
What does that even feel like?

69
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,520
No matter how much money I have,

70
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:13,200
I won't be happy

71
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,880
if a ghost keeps haunting me like this.

72
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:18,080
If you have this much money,

73
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,560
why don't you move away from the ghost?

74
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:22,840
Move to Switzerland or Korea.

75
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,920
A ghost can't get through immigration.

76
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:27,080
The ghost isn't haunting the house,

77
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,800
and it isn't following me either.

78
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,240
It only appears
when I'm with my boyfriend.

79
00:05:31,320 --> 00:05:33,120
I never know when it'll show up.

80
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,760
There's no pattern at all.

81
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,000
And it can go anywhere.

82
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,400
You said it couldn't
get through immigration?

83
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:40,800
So where am I supposed to run?

84
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,360
Okay.

85
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,680
If that's really the case,

86
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:48,600
I'll make that ghost run for its life.

87
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,160
But the thing is,

88
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,800
for the ghost to appear,

89
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:54,400
you'd have to be my boyfriend first.

90
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,400
Wait, so I'm not just negotiating
with the ghost?

91
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,560
I have to pretend to be
your boyfriend to fool it too?

92
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:01,640
We'll trick it into coming out first,

93
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:03,560
then you can chase it away.

94
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,600
Linda told me

95
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,480
you often work as a fake boyfriend.

96
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,200
This is just another job. Right?

97
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,400
But are you sure

98
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,640
if we put on an act,

99
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:17,960
the ghost will be dumb enough to
believe us and come out?

100
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,960
You just have to make it convincing enough

101
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,240
for it to believe us.

102
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,960
I've connected every device to
our room's Wi-Fi.

103
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:35,640
And I'm syncing the data to
the cloud server in real time.

104
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,400
If any energy wave interferes,

105
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,120
the system will alert us immediately.

106
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,200
Wow.

107
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:43,400
You look really nerdy.

108
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,640
That's not all.

109
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,840
This measures physiological responses.

110
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,480
I'll use you as a warning radar.

111
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,080
When this pen goes off,

112
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,240
it means the ghost is here.

113
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,560
So I'll be ready to curse it out.

114
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,880
Unbutton your shirt a little.

115
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,920
Just two buttons.

116
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,040
What?

117
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,520
Just hurry up and do it.
Don't ask questions.

118
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:00,800
You're all set.

119
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,040
The graph's spiking this much.

120
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,720
Does… Does it mean the ghost is here?

121
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,720
This thing must be sensitive.

122
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,600
Show me.

123
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:20,120
Where did you last see it?

124
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:24,560
Here.

125
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,840
- Here?
- Yeah.

126
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,160
What were you doing then?

127
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:36,799
At the time, I…

128
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:38,520
<i>I was kissing my boyfriend.</i>

129
00:08:39,559 --> 00:08:41,360
<i>He was about to kiss me.</i>

130
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,360
Shit!

131
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,400
Kan, where are you going?

132
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,720
Enough, enough.

133
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,360
What about before that?

134
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:01,840
What else happens when the ghost appears?

135
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,360
Tell me about it.

136
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,760
Before that…

137
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,160
- Get out!
- Shit!

138
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:21,480
What's wrong?

139
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,920
Nothing's wrong.

140
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:29,120
Why did you hit me on the head?

141
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,720
I didn't.

142
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:34,000
If it wasn't you, who else could it be?

143
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:37,000
Don't bother me anymore.

144
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,440
That's why I've never
had a serious relationship.

145
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:42,400
I've gone to see monks
from many different places.

146
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:45,120
I've made merit to atone for my karma.
I've tried everything.

147
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,560
This time, it'll definitely disappear.

148
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,920
I'll make sure of it.

149
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,920
I'm determined to finish this job.

150
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,480
Because you feel sorry for me?

151
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:55,240
No. I'm doing it for the money.

152
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,600
I have a reason
I need one million baht soon.

153
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,840
So I'll need your cooperation
as the client.

154
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:10,760
We agreed to pretend to be a couple.

155
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,760
Oh.

156
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,480
If you're easily affected,

157
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,200
these graphs won't be very accurate.

158
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,640
You need to toughen up a little.

159
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,640
Try taking a deep breath.

160
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:50,080
Then sit and wait for the ghost
to come haunt you.

161
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:56,800
But I don't know
if the ghost will come out.

162
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,280
You said the ghost doesn't want you
to have a partner, right?

163
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,680
We just…

164
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:04,960
We just provoke the ghost.

165
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,120
What do I have to do?

166
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,920
Put some effort into it.

167
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,120
Again.

168
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,440
Looks like it'll take quite a while.

169
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,200
I'll probably have to
move in here temporarily.

170
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:07,120
Is that okay?

171
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,640
Sure.

172
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:10,080
When will you move in?

173
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:11,720
Tonight works.

174
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,840
I understand that
we have to pretend to be a couple.

175
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,440
But can bedtime count as a break?

176
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:53,040
You keep moving closer to me.

177
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,600
Are you a person or a worm?

178
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:56,560
Move over.

179
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:02,920
I'm a light sleeper.

180
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,440
If anything touches me,
I really can't sleep.

181
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:15,120
This side is a you-free zone.

182
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,120
If you cross over,
I'll charge you ten thousand each time.

183
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,440
I can actually afford that.

184
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,040
You're really persistent.

185
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,760
Good night.

186
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,160
What happened?

187
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,720
Is there a fire?

188
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:53,680
It's time for our
romance-to-lure-a-ghost mission.

189
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,800
Hurry up and get up.

190
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,280
Let me sleep for another ten minutes.

191
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,840
No.

192
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:02,440
Five minutes, then.

193
00:14:03,040 --> 00:14:05,360
Vann, didn't you say you wanted to
finish this mission quickly?

194
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,400
Come on.

195
00:14:06,920 --> 00:14:08,960
Wake up.

196
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:12,520
Are you crazy?

197
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,720
Who the hell wakes up to flirt this early?

198
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,200
Me.

199
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:17,760
Get out of bed.

200
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,480
Come on.

201
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,560
Vann, get out of bed.

202
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,560
<i>Vann.</i>

203
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:32,680
Vann.

204
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:35,880
- Vann.
- What?

205
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,000
Is the ghost here?

206
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:39,080
Come on, let's go running.

207
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,960
Wait, wait.

208
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,360
Are you okay?

209
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,440
You don't have to.

210
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:10,320
But…

211
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,520
you can wipe it for me.

212
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:13,880
Make it sweet.

213
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,960
Okay, do it.

214
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:35,640
Do you see anything?

215
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:38,640
I don't.

216
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,320
Vann, let's take a picture together.

217
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,400
No matter how you look at it,
we don't look like a couple.

218
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,480
Don't you think?

219
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,320
Yeah.

220
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,320
Let's not do this activity anymore.

221
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:05,640
It's not working.

222
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,680
Vann, try this.

223
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,120
The coffee here is good.

224
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:14,040
No.

225
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,720
If you want me to try it,
go get a new straw.

226
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:17,840
Come on, Vann.

227
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:20,240
We're a couple,
so we have to use the same straw.

228
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,600
Just a little.

229
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,680
So cute.

230
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,640
How is this supposed to fool a ghost?

231
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:40,240
You can't even fool a person with that.

232
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,040
This is how you do it.

233
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,960
Hey, why didn't you take the picture?

234
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,960
- Okay.
- Take another one.

235
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,440
Where's the ghost?

236
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:27,520
Maybe our acting still
isn't convincing enough.

237
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:29,080
I'm leaving.

238
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,480
We've been together for hours.

239
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,320
The ghost still hasn't shown up.

240
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,240
Even a dog could tell we're not close.

241
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,080
It's forced, Vann.

242
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,400
Let me ask you seriously.

243
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:49,800
Have you ever been in love?

244
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,200
That's personal.
Nothing to do with the job.

245
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,320
Why are you asking?

246
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,200
Of course it has to do with the job.

247
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:58,840
We have to fool the ghost into
thinking we're a couple.

248
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,040
But you don't seem to
understand love at all.

249
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,600
So what's a good
boyfriend supposed to be like?

250
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,680
Do I have to remember your size?

251
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:07,840
And when you forget condoms,
do I have to rush out to buy them?

252
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:10,000
You keep reminding me.
I remember your size.

253
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:11,240
Hey!

254
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:12,760
Calm down.

255
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:21,640
Hey.

256
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,760
Are you that pervert
from the elevator that day?

257
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,600
Yes.

258
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,000
That's me.

259
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:31,080
But let me say something.

260
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,400
In the end, no matter
how much you indulge him,

261
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,040
when he's in serious trouble,

262
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:37,200
your boyfriend
still leaves you, doesn't he?

263
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:39,400
What do you know?

264
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,320
You've never even had a boyfriend before.

265
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:45,160
And now you're acting like
you know everything?

266
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:48,640
Hey. Don't be mad.

267
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:51,000
If you're not ready to understand love,

268
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,160
then don't say anything.

269
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,920
I'm just going by theory.

270
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,320
In theory, good love should be like this.

271
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,880
Stop rambling about theories
that don't fucking work.

272
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,720
Because they don't work in practice.

273
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:04,440
I think we should stop here for today.

274
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,480
I need some time alone to think.

275
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,760
Hey.

276
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:09,880
Aren't you afraid of the ghost anymore?

277
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,160
It's fine.

278
00:19:11,240 --> 00:19:13,600
If I'm alone, the ghost won't appear.

279
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:17,360
Or maybe I'll have to fucking
live alone like this forever.

280
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:20,720
Hey, wait!

281
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,960
He says he's not mad,
but I think he clearly is.

282
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,920
This is Nugget's new home.

283
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,040
What is this?

284
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:39,080
Egg cartons help diffuse sound waves

285
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:41,320
and soak up noise so it doesn't leak out.

286
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,200
That's amazing.

287
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:50,680
It does keep the sound in,

288
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,280
but I wonder…

289
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:56,000
will it be able to breathe?

290
00:19:56,080 --> 00:19:59,520
Doesn't it look too cramped and stuffy?

291
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,760
Hey,

292
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,360
I think

293
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,200
in theory, it might work.

294
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:10,120
But in practice,

295
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,680
I don't think it'll work.

296
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:14,840
How would I know? I've never had one.

297
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:16,520
Never had what?

298
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:17,480
A boyf…

299
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:21,280
I mean, I've never been a chick.

300
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:22,800
I've never been a chick either.

301
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,160
No one's ever been a chick.

302
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:26,560
There you guys are.

303
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,000
What are you doing? Reading cards again?

304
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:31,240
Yeah, here.

305
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:33,560
- What's this?
- Don't touch it, Linda.

306
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,000
This is my new product.

307
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,120
Don't mess with it.

308
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,960
You're that protective of it?

309
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,600
And how's the job with Rakkhun going?

310
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:45,400
Great.

311
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:48,600
The chemistry between me and him
is really good.

312
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,400
I guarantee this job will be
done ahead of schedule.

313
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,440
It's good that you two
have great chemistry.

314
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,440
Because if you screw up this job,

315
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:00,960
I guarantee you'll be
a waiter here until you die.

316
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:03,040
You probably won't make it to Japan.

317
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:19,880
<i>Vann, what are you doing?</i>

318
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:29,400
<i>So basically,</i>

319
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,640
you told your client off,

320
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:33,240
so he got upset.

321
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:34,680
Then he just disappeared.

322
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,840
Yeah.

323
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,760
I just criticized him based on
what I thought.

324
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:41,360
But when I saw Nugget just now,

325
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,680
I realized

326
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,240
you can't rely on theory alone
for things like this.

327
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:47,760
If I don't experience it myself,
I won't know.

328
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:49,360
You're screwed.

329
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:52,520
I think you should confess to Linda

330
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:54,640
that your client ran away from you.

331
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,640
- Go.
- No.

332
00:21:56,720 --> 00:21:58,160
I don't want to give up.

333
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:00,240
If you don't want to give up,

334
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:02,160
you have to go apologize to him

335
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:04,440
and tell him, "I was wrong."

336
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:07,320
But he told me he wanted to be alone.

337
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,760
Let me tell you something.

338
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:13,400
When people are a couple
and they're upset,

339
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
they'll say, "I want to be alone."

340
00:22:16,520 --> 00:22:18,560
- But no one actually wants to be alone.
- Yeah.

341
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:21,000
And no one leaves their
partner alone either.

342
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:21,920
Except you.

343
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:25,880
He's just my fake boyfriend.

344
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,840
Guys. Rakkhun messaged me.

345
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,600
You're screwed. I don't even need
to read the cards to know.

346
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:42,200
You're definitely getting fired.
You're done for.

347
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:44,280
Did he message you to fire you?

348
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:47,480
Shit, that mouth of yours.

349
00:22:47,560 --> 00:22:48,440
‪RAKKHUN

350
00:22:48,520 --> 00:22:51,400
<i>Vann. What are you doing?</i>

351
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,360
Guys.

352
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,080
I survived. My job's not canceled yet.

353
00:22:58,680 --> 00:22:59,640
I'm off.

354
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:01,640
My funds for Japan are waiting for me.

355
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:03,360
I'm going.

356
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:11,480
Why did you call me here?

357
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,720
Are you going to fire me?

358
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:15,640
No.

359
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,800
You looked really angry with me earlier,

360
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:21,520
so I thought you were going to fire me.

361
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,160
It was my fault.

362
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,880
I don't know what I was thinking then.

363
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:42,280
Maybe I was angry because
you hit a nerve about my exes.

364
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,840
Because I know sometimes
it wasn't really love.

365
00:23:47,040 --> 00:23:49,240
But I just want to have
a good relationship

366
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:50,760
like everyone else.

367
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:51,920
- I just…
- Enough.

368
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:54,520
You don't have to say anything else.

369
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:57,320
I'm the one who should apologize.

370
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:01,960
I don't really know your
happiness or your pain,

371
00:24:02,040 --> 00:24:04,480
yet I had the nerve to judge your life.

372
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,840
I'm sorry I left you alone.

373
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:10,080
Can we…

374
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:11,880
Can we make up?

375
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:23,120
So we're good now, right?

376
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:26,160
We're good.

377
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:29,360
From now on,
I'm running the system for real.

378
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:31,960
Vann.

379
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:35,040
Thank you so much.

380
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,800
Don't worry.

381
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:40,480
Tomorrow, I'll take you on
an organic-style date.

382
00:24:41,360 --> 00:24:43,120
I guarantee the ghost will come out.

383
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,000
Come in a little more.
You're almost there.

384
00:24:57,400 --> 00:24:59,240
You brought me for an ice bath?

385
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:00,720
Yeah.

386
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:03,760
It helps with muscles
and reduces injuries.

387
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:07,080
And it makes our hearts race like
when we fall in love at first sight.

388
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,040
You want me to soak in an ice bath?

389
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:12,200
I've never done this.

390
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:13,960
Won't I die from shock?

391
00:25:15,520 --> 00:25:18,480
If you could die from this,
plenty of people would've died before you.

392
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:20,320
This won't kill you.

393
00:25:20,920 --> 00:25:23,040
Anything you've never done, try it all.

394
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,080
How do you feel? Is your heart racing?

395
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:41,800
My heart's about to stop instead.

396
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,240
You got this.

397
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,120
This is the date you planned?

398
00:25:56,760 --> 00:25:59,040
Where's your sense of romance?

399
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:01,880
This is a date. We're up this high.

400
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,840
There's no way your heart won't race.

401
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:05,720
Your heart rate graph will spike,

402
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:07,600
and maybe the ghost
will finally come haunt us.

403
00:26:09,040 --> 00:26:10,280
Let me see.

404
00:26:24,760 --> 00:26:26,560
- Are we starting now?
- Yeah.

405
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:43,400
Vann, I can't do this.

406
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:45,240
It's too high.

407
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,360
Trust me.

408
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,680
I won't let you fall.

409
00:27:01,760 --> 00:27:03,160
Thank you so much.

410
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,360
Vann!

411
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:08,120
Wait!

412
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:15,800
That was so much fun.

413
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:17,400
I didn't think I could climb it.

414
00:27:22,520 --> 00:27:24,320
See? Just like that.

415
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:26,080
Your heart really is racing.

416
00:27:31,280 --> 00:27:32,280
Let's get up.

417
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:36,280
Up.

418
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,600
I'm hungry.

419
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:44,280
Is there anything I can eat
that'll make my heart race?

420
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,640
Sure.

421
00:27:45,720 --> 00:27:48,040
I guarantee your heart will
burst right out of your chest.

422
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:50,560
Come on. I'll take you there.

423
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:57,000
Raw buffalo larb!

424
00:27:57,600 --> 00:28:00,760
It's so hard to find food
from my hometown.

425
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:03,400
But how did you find this place?

426
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:05,560
I looked up your family history.

427
00:28:05,640 --> 00:28:07,920
You're from an old family in Lamphun.

428
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,200
I thought this place would suit you.

429
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:12,200
So I asked Linda to call the owner
and bump you up the waitlist.

430
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:14,600
Try it.

431
00:28:15,960 --> 00:28:17,480
Then I won't hold back.

432
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:22,040
You should eat with me.

433
00:29:03,040 --> 00:29:05,480
You're working for me.
How could I let you pay?

434
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:07,400
I'm not here to work.

435
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:09,080
I'm here on a date today.

436
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:13,560
Hey, is that your ex?

437
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,160
Done.

438
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:20,600
Keep the change.

439
00:29:21,440 --> 00:29:23,800
You paid by QR code,
so there isn't any change.

440
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:38,240
What do you think of this bracelet?

441
00:29:38,320 --> 00:29:39,480
Is it pretty?

442
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:41,720
It's well-crafted.

443
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:44,160
Hey, be honest.

444
00:29:46,400 --> 00:29:47,480
I'd say it's pretty.

445
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:49,280
If it were ugly, I'd tell you.

446
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:53,880
Do you like wearing silver
because you're from the North?

447
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:58,040
Yeah, but my family
is next-level Yong people.

448
00:29:58,120 --> 00:29:59,680
As for worshipping ancestral spirits,

449
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:01,720
it's like the Chinese Ghost Festival

450
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,440
or how we Thais worship our ancestors.

451
00:30:03,520 --> 00:30:05,720
The ancestral spirits help
ward off bad things.

452
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:07,920
They help keep misfortune away
from their descendants.

453
00:30:18,040 --> 00:30:19,120
What's special about this necklace?

454
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:21,240
This looks like Kan's.

455
00:30:22,480 --> 00:30:23,520
My boyfriend.

456
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:27,240
That coward?

457
00:30:27,320 --> 00:30:29,400
Hey, don't talk about him like that.

458
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:31,640
He didn't mean to run away from me.

459
00:30:31,720 --> 00:30:33,360
He was running from the ghost.

460
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:36,800
I think your ex might be a bad guy.

461
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:38,360
That's why the ghost chased him away.

462
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,720
Kan is sweet.

463
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:44,560
He was really good to me.

464
00:30:45,240 --> 00:30:46,760
If we can sort out the ghost problem,

465
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:49,440
I'd like to ask Kan to get back together.

466
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:52,280
I don't know if I'll still have a chance.

467
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:41,040
Vann, did you buy me the bracelet?

468
00:31:42,600 --> 00:31:43,920
Why are you confused?

469
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:45,800
You wanted it, so I bought it for you.

470
00:31:48,840 --> 00:31:49,800
You bought me something.

471
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:52,400
Is that included in the
organic date package too?

472
00:31:54,880 --> 00:31:57,640
What if I wear it and only think of you?

473
00:31:58,440 --> 00:31:59,280
What am I supposed to do?

474
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:10,800
I don't mind.

475
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:12,720
It's good if you think of me
instead of Kan.

476
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:14,280
What?

477
00:32:14,880 --> 00:32:16,080
What do you mean?

478
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:19,000
I know I'm no love expert,

479
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:20,880
but I think

480
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:22,320
loving each other

481
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,920
means supporting each other always.

482
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:26,320
So if we love each other,

483
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,640
no matter what problems you face,

484
00:32:29,240 --> 00:32:30,600
I'll never run away

485
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:32,080
and leave you alone.

486
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:35,680
From now on, if you're sad,

487
00:32:35,760 --> 00:32:37,120
look at this bracelet

488
00:32:37,720 --> 00:32:39,320
and think of me instead.

489
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,360
You don't have to think of anyone else.

490
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:43,840
Do you understand?

491
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:56,800
Thank you.

492
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:00,440
‪Of course.

493
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:11,640
‪VANN

494
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:13,440
<i>Is the bracelet I gave you</i>
<i>comfortable to wear?</i>

495
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:21,560
<i>No, my hand gets swollen</i>
<i>and itchy when I wear it.</i>

496
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,640
<i>Is it fake silver?</i>

497
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:24,440
<i>It's real silver.</i>

498
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:26,400
<i>It's premium, just like the person</i>
<i>who gave it to you.</i>

499
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:36,440
<i>It's Friday. Buy me a beer.</i>

500
00:33:36,960 --> 00:33:39,200
<i>Whoever invites the other person pays.</i>

501
00:33:39,280 --> 00:33:40,320
<i>You said it yourself, and you forgot.</i>

502
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:46,840
<i>Fine, I'll pay. Will you come meet me?</i>

503
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:06,360
<i>I want to see you,</i>
<i>but I'm not done with work yet.</i>

504
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:08,639
<i>Can I call you instead?</i>

505
00:34:09,639 --> 00:34:12,480
Hello, Vann. What are you doing?

506
00:34:12,560 --> 00:34:14,520
I'm in my room. Where else would I be?

507
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,360
Where are you?

508
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:28,440
- Let's take a break.
- Hot sausages are here.

509
00:34:28,520 --> 00:34:30,560
- They look so good.
- Ladies first.

510
00:34:30,639 --> 00:34:32,440
- Thank you.
- Okay.

511
00:34:32,520 --> 00:34:34,600
- I'll have one too.
- Thank you.

512
00:34:34,679 --> 00:34:36,520
- So damn lucky. A guy's cooking for me.
- Here.

513
00:34:36,600 --> 00:34:38,440
- Talay, want one?
- Thanks.

514
00:34:38,520 --> 00:34:39,760
You gave me a whole one.

515
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,199
Tell me.

516
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,719
Do you guys think he's acting normal?

517
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:46,000
I've never seen this side of him.

518
00:34:46,679 --> 00:34:48,560
Maybe he's ordering a new dinosaur figure.

519
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:52,440
Vann, are you this happy
while working these days?

520
00:34:52,520 --> 00:34:54,199
- Exactly.
- Yeah.

521
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:57,040
You usually look so dead inside
when talking to clients.

522
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:58,600
What's gotten into you, Vann?

523
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:01,040
I'm discussing a million-baht deal.

524
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:03,320
- Don't bother me.
- Yeah, let's leave him alone.

525
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,480
Let's just eat.

526
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:08,680
Talay.

527
00:35:08,760 --> 00:35:09,680
- What?
- So good.

528
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:10,920
Can I borrow your car?

529
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:14,520
Just get a ride.

530
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:15,640
Why do you need my car?

531
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,920
I don't want my hair
getting all messed up.

532
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:18,920
I'll drive your car.

533
00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:21,280
Now he's obsessed with looking good.

534
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:22,520
No.

535
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,520
Linda said I'm the youngest.

536
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:26,280
Aren't you guys supposed to
take care of me?

537
00:35:28,120 --> 00:35:29,160
I'm borrowing your car.

538
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:33,280
Fine.

539
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:36,360
Drive it carefully.

540
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:44,880
Vann, aren't you eating?

541
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:47,520
- No. You guys eat. I'm leaving.
- Hey!

542
00:35:50,840 --> 00:35:52,200
I didn't mean to do that.

543
00:35:53,080 --> 00:35:55,040
If that's all you're
going to say, just go.

544
00:35:55,120 --> 00:35:56,640
Just go. Go.

545
00:35:56,720 --> 00:35:58,000
Hear me out first.

546
00:35:58,080 --> 00:35:59,440
- What else do you want me to hear?
- Rak.

547
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,840
Rak, hold this for a second.

548
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:08,720
Wait, Rakkhun.

549
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:09,800
Rak.

550
00:36:10,600 --> 00:36:11,440
Just a second, Rak.

551
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,760
Can you stay and talk to me for a second?

552
00:36:15,520 --> 00:36:16,520
What is it?

553
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:18,400
Well…

554
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:20,960
That night, I was just shocked.

555
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:24,120
It's okay.

556
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:26,760
Anyone would be shocked by
something like that.

557
00:36:26,840 --> 00:36:28,160
It's normal.

558
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:29,160
I understand.

559
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:32,720
Thanks so much for understanding me.

560
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,440
Well…

561
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:42,640
I…

562
00:36:43,280 --> 00:36:45,400
I didn't want to break up with you.

563
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:49,880
It was just a small mishap at the time.

564
00:36:52,040 --> 00:36:53,760
Right now, technically…

565
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:55,840
we're still together, right?

566
00:37:00,480 --> 00:37:01,960
Well…

567
00:37:03,840 --> 00:37:05,480
You don't want to be with me anymore?

568
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:08,480
It's not that.

569
00:37:09,320 --> 00:37:10,400
Well…

570
00:37:21,600 --> 00:37:23,880
How much longer are you going to
make me wait? I want to go home.

571
00:37:25,400 --> 00:37:27,720
My brother is here to pick me up.

572
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,600
I'll tell you once I have an answer.

573
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,240
Didn't you say you couldn't pick me up?

574
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:42,120
Didn't you tell me yesterday you had
no one to help you with your model?

575
00:37:42,200 --> 00:37:43,480
I'll help you today.

576
00:37:43,560 --> 00:37:46,520
I can build it myself.

577
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:48,480
I can stay with my friend
another night. It's fine.

578
00:37:48,560 --> 00:37:50,720
It's fine. Let's go.

579
00:38:12,880 --> 00:38:13,800
Hurry up and eat.

580
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:15,800
Your hands are shaking from hunger.
You almost cut yourself.

581
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:18,920
I'm not eating. I'm in a hurry.

582
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,440
You said you'd help me with my model.

583
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:25,040
If you lied to me today,

584
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:27,320
I'll tell Linda.

585
00:38:28,600 --> 00:38:29,480
I don't care.

586
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:32,280
If you won't eat, I won't help you.

587
00:38:42,560 --> 00:38:43,960
Fine, I'll eat.

588
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:56,960
You'll definitely get your work done.

589
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:58,920
I don't make promises I can't keep.

590
00:39:17,360 --> 00:39:18,640
I'm going to wash my hands.

591
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:20,440
Vann.

592
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:31,920
Kan came to talk to me.

593
00:39:33,360 --> 00:39:36,040
He apologized and said
he was just shocked back then.

594
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:38,520
And he also told me

595
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:39,920
he still loves me.

596
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:41,960
What do you think I should do?

597
00:39:44,960 --> 00:39:47,240
You want to get back
together with him, don't you?

598
00:39:50,040 --> 00:39:51,680
But if I get back together with him,

599
00:39:51,760 --> 00:39:54,720
I don't know if he'll leave me again
when he sees the ghost.

600
00:39:55,360 --> 00:39:57,680
Then hurry up and finish the model
for your professor,

601
00:39:58,280 --> 00:40:00,080
so we can get back to focusing on
the ghost-hunting mission,

602
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:02,200
and I can get my job done sooner.

603
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:04,520
Then, you can get back together with him.

604
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:05,600
Sound good?

605
00:40:06,840 --> 00:40:08,680
I hope that's how it turns out.

606
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,160
Hurry up and do it.

607
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:12,920
- Go on.
- I am.

608
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:42,040
<i>Don't you have to be on campus</i>
<i>to build your model tonight?</i>

609
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:43,520
<i>Can I come see you?</i>

610
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:48,280
<i>That's okay. I want to do it alone.</i>

611
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,360
If you can't stay up, go to sleep first.

612
00:41:21,440 --> 00:41:22,560
I'll do the rest.

613
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:25,520
You're even better at it than me.

614
00:41:26,520 --> 00:41:28,280
Didn't you say you studied engineering?

615
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:32,360
Some things, you're just born with.

616
00:41:32,440 --> 00:41:33,680
It's called talent.

617
00:41:34,320 --> 00:41:36,840
Next time you have
another model to build, just hire me

618
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:38,840
so you won't have to work so hard.

619
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:41,280
I'm sleepy.

620
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,600
I can't stay awake anymore.

621
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:51,840
Go to sleep.

622
00:42:03,920 --> 00:42:05,280
Get some sleep.

623
00:42:05,360 --> 00:42:06,400
I'll wake you when it's done.

624
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:09,600
Aren't you going to sleep?

625
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:13,640
I stay up late every night anyway.

626
00:42:17,520 --> 00:42:18,920
I'm just worried about you.

627
00:42:20,880 --> 00:42:22,160
Thanks, Vann.

628
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:25,240
You're really good to me.

629
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:35,240
Do you see it?

630
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:37,960
Is that the ghost?

631
00:43:39,720 --> 00:43:41,960
Why are you scared? I'm here.

632
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,640
As for the ghost,

633
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:47,080
it should be scared of me.

634
00:44:02,960 --> 00:44:04,760
Get ready for a "nice to meet you,"

635
00:44:04,840 --> 00:44:05,920
you stupid ghost.

636
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:52,040
- Do you trust me, Rak?
- Of course I do.

637
00:44:52,120 --> 00:44:53,440
<i>Then I’m sorry.</i>

638
00:44:53,520 --> 00:44:54,840
You’re kinda naughty too.

639
00:44:54,920 --> 00:44:56,160
I even lit incense,
and you didn’t show up.

640
00:44:56,240 --> 00:44:57,680
But you suddenly showed up
when we started kissing.

641
00:44:58,440 --> 00:44:59,600
<i>Vann!</i>

642
00:45:00,240 --> 00:45:01,720
Do you want to audition
to be a singer here?

643
00:45:01,800 --> 00:45:02,640
Yes, I do.

644
00:45:02,720 --> 00:45:05,800
<i>So this is one of the ways</i>
<i>you’re trying to convince Phatee</i>

645
00:45:05,880 --> 00:45:07,240
<i>to take your job, right?</i>

646
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:10,240
We’ll have to work together
someday anyway, right?

647
00:45:10,320 --> 00:45:12,600
Just try to get along.

648
00:45:15,720 --> 00:45:17,080
<i>Kind.</i>

649
00:45:17,160 --> 00:45:18,040
<i>Comforting.</i>

650
00:45:18,120 --> 00:45:19,920
You’ve got such a male lead vibe.
